ter or a day later or a year  later and so you can really go through  things at your own pace and so  we don't view video conferencing as  maybe our main delivery mechanism  although distance learning um you know  vendors or companies or schools might  view video conferencing as their main  way to get to people we think hey we can  record videos they can  people can consume those at their own  pace and we can give people exercises  and feedback that they can they can do  at their own base where we do  think video conferencing could be really  really really interesting this is  something that we have not that we have  not done yet we've kind of thrown around  the idea and we just really have to get  the bandwidth to address it  is  i think video conferencing is a  is an amazing way to have peer-to-peer  interactions  so peer-to-peer i'll just do the acronym  peer-to-peer interactions so right now  in a lot of the classrooms that are  piloting khan academy or even the ones  that are doing it on their own  and this is what we really advocate is  every student works at their own pace  but when they're stuck either the  teacher intervenes based on the data  that the teacher sees or even better a  student intervenes and helps their peer  and we think that that can that there's  no reason why that has to be sit just in  a physical classroom that you could  actually transcend a physical classroom  and that's where something like video  conferencing could be really valuable if  two people could share a blackboard that  looks very similar like this and they  have either a tablet device or a pen  tablet like what i'm using right now  they can run a tutoring session with  each other it would even be cool if they  could record it and it could be archived  for for other people uh to use it in the  future so so that is is really powerful  and that's mainly in the tutoring space  so that you can have peer-to-peer  tutoring  tutoring or really teaching or mentoring  even and the other interesting place  where peer-to-peer interactions could be  interesting i think this is completely  untapped is the whole idea of assessment  right now khan academy the assessment  piece happens you're doing exercises it  keeps track of how you're doing  in a traditional classroom assessments  are some form of paper exam it could be  multiple choice could be free answer it  could be essay exam but what i think  most of us have always appre realized is  that the most the highest form of  assessment is either the practical  assessment or the oral assessment so  practical would literally mean you know  if you're if you're starting to be a  nurse someone observe you while you're  trying to you know insert an iv into  someone's into someone's  arm and oral examination and this is  really the gold standard for what we see  in the academia is look when you're when  you're going through your qualifiers  there's an oral part of that examination  and then essentially you'll sit in front  of a room full of faculty members and  they'll grill you on and make sure you  really really really do understand a  concept deeply and so what we think we  could do where on the peer-to-peer side  is eventually have not only just the  kind of assessment that we already have  in place at khan academy but maybe an  oral assessment where you know right now  maybe you are a we don't have the proper  words for it but maybe you are a level  one  you're level one in trigonometry or  level one in algebra and you wanna go  you to become level 2 in trigonometry  you want to get into this this like a  smaller circle this more elite circle of  people who've gotten to this deep level  of trigonometry and to do that maybe on  a baseline you have to do some you have  to show that you've done something on  kind of the traditional exercises on  khan academy at your own pace and and  you've been able to prove competency  there but to really make it then you  would have an oral examination with  maybe five people from level two  five people from level two and if maybe  four out of the five say that you are  ready for level two then you will be  bumped up to level two and then one of  your responsibilities is someone in  level two is it to  assess future people for level from  level one coming from level one and then  of course then your next aspiration is  to go to level three or go become a  master of all of the math or whatever  you might want to say so i think  peer-to-peer interactions could be  really really powerful when it comes to  the assessment part i think you know i'd  be hard-pressed to see how this isn't  more rigorous than really all the  assessment that has in place because  you're all you're not just being  assessed by arbitrary peers you're being  assessed by peers who've already really  proven themselves to to really deeply  understand the concept  the other things um  you know when you say is is this  is this that's something that he sees  the khan academy using and what kind of  timeframe well once again we do see  ourselves using it but we don't know the  time frame it's just a bandwidth issue  and oh that reminds me so the other area  where i think video conferencing could  be really powerful is in the idea of  foreign language so once again the gold  standard in foreign language is really  immersion but uh that's obviously not  always possible or economically possible  but the second best thing to immersion  is actually having live interactions  with people on the other side of the  world or maybe even not on the other  side of the world  you know one thing i want to do with my  two and a half year old is maybe get him  a skype or maybe a google plus buddy or  whatever it is  in different countries so that he can  start chatting with kids maybe his own  age or a little older a little younger  and they can just start to at least get  the basics of each other's languages and  start to teach each other so i think it  has it could have a lot to be done in  not full immersion but pseudo immersion  in for for foreign language for foreign  language learning and then a lot of the  core for the foreign language like the  vocabulary and the grammar  we could probably do our exercise  platform but this is really what gives  you that deeper understanding of it  the next question is is there a  possibility of khan academy's  qualifications achievements being  externally validated at some point such  that they're recognized internationally  as a measure of academic achievement so  there definitely is a possibility and we  are exploring to see to see how  what  how can we validate that when someone  does something on khan academy that is  really coming from them and we think  there are ways to do it we could even  have you know places where you could go  and you could show your id or whatever  and say hey look this is me um i'm not  going to do the khan academy there and  then we could validate yes this was  definitely the person who who did that  and then once you do that we could we  could we we could give badges or  validations that look this person really  does know that information and then it's  it's a matter of making sure that they  are accepted um broadly and i think this  actually touches on a generalized  problem  in that right now you have and i've  talked about this in in other videos and  other  lectures right now education is kind of  a mixture of you have the learning part  you have the learning part you have the  credentialing part  credentialing part and then you have a  little bit of a socialization part  socialization you have a little bit of  socialization and when you go to a  university and you pay the big tuition  you're kind of you know you're getting  all of this stuff and depending who you  ask different people think they're  paying for providing different things if  you ask most students at most  universities they're probably most  focused on the credential but if you ask  most of the universities they'll say hey  no all of our resources are going to  this right over here the credential is  just to make sure that you know people  are going the  are are learning the things but they're  actually spending the resources over  here and so that question i think about  whether khan academy can give  credentials or frankly whether third  party can get credentials i think is  just the whole issue of can we decouple  this can we separate can we se can we  create a line of separation between the  learning side of education and the  credentialing side and i think if you do  that generally something really powerful  happens if we can create and it doesn't  have to come from khan academy it can  come from a government it could come  from ngos it could come from who knows  where it comes from if there is an  internationally recognized battery of  examinations  assessments and deep assessments they  can be practical they could be oral they  could be paper based all of the above  and so if you have something like this  that is internationally recognized  then all of a sudden the rest of the  education world will compete right over  here and then their students will just  try to get this thing right over here  and what's exciting about something like  that is then khan academy could compete  on equal footing because if students who  choose to go through khan academy for  free perform just as well on that as the  student who's you know spending tens of  thousands of dollars then or maybe  certain students who say well this just  works better for me or maybe some  students will just learn on the job  they'll learn on the job or they'll  learn from textbooks but it allows  students to learn the best way they can  the best way that fits their career and  even their economic situation and the  other good thing is if this is  internationally recognized it solves the  problem that  right now there are some big name  schools that if you are if you're if  you're lucky enough to 